  "caption": "This figure is a diagnostic of the metric, not a comparison of the grids: cycle-mean R² is computed on each grid's own 6 holdout configurations as 1 − ε²/σ², where σ is the population standard deviation of the true cycle means and ε the RMS error of the predicted ones. Left: the waveform RMS (the scale pointwise R² sees), σ, and ε for each of the 5 seeds, ε = σ·√(1 − R²); where ε ≥ σ, R² ≤ 0. Right: the 5 per-seed R² values; 5 seeds give the observed spread, not a confidence interval. Shows the shipped surrogate (surrogate/). Targets are lab-frame components of the IB force and moment on the wing; moments about the hinge. Holdout rows are the second wingbeat of 2-beat runs; the corpus is to be regenerated with longer runs."
